        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Consider the following equation:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2{\\color{red}m}{\\color{blue}t} = 1]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Consider the following equation:\n[MATH: 2{\\color{red}m}{\\color{blue}t} = 1]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Notice that this equation has two variables, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}m}]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}t}.]</span> Suppose we want to solve the equation for the variable <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}t}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Notice that this equation has two variables, [MATH: {\\color{red}m}] and [MATH: {\\color{blue}t}.] Suppose we want to solve the equation for the variable [MATH: {\\color{blue}t}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To isolate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}t},]</span> we apply the multiplication principle and divide both sides of the equation by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2{\\color{red}m},]</span> treating <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}m}]</span> as though it were a constant:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To isolate [MATH: {\\color{blue}t},] we apply the multiplication principle and divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 2{\\color{red}m},] treating [MATH: {\\color{red}m}] as though it were a constant:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2mt|= 1; (2mt)/(2m)|= (1)/(2m); (2mt)/(2m)|= (1)/(2m); t|= (1)/(2m)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 2mt|= 1; (2mt)/(2m)|= (1)/(2m); (2mt)/(2m)|= (1)/(2m); t|= (1)/(2m)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Next, we&#x27;ll take a look at an example where we need to apply both the addition and multiplication principles.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Next, we'll take a look at an example where we need to apply both the addition and multiplication principles.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nConsider the following equation:\n[MATH: 2{\\color{red}m}{\\color{blue}t} = 1]\n\nContent:\nNotice that this equation has two variables, [MATH: {\\color{red}m}] and [MATH: {\\color{blue}t}.] Suppose we want to solve the equation for the variable [MATH: {\\color{blue}t}.]\n\nContent:\nTo isolate [MATH: {\\color{blue}t},] we apply the multiplication principle and divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 2{\\color{red}m},] treating [MATH: {\\color{red}m}] as though it were a constant:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2mt|= 1; (2mt)/(2m)|= (1)/(2m); (2mt)/(2m)|= (1)/(2m); t|= (1)/(2m)]\n\nContent:\nNext, we'll take a look at an example where we need to apply both the addition and multiplication principles."
      },
