            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Solve the equation <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 34 kx + 9 = 2]</span> for the variable <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Solve the equation [MATH: \\dfrac 34 kx + 9 = 2] for the variable [MATH: x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we multiply both sides of the equation by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> to get rid of the fraction:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (3)/(4)kx + 9|= 2; 4 \u22c5 ((3)/(4)kx + 9)|= 4 \u22c5 2; 3kx + 36|= 8]</span></p><p>Now, we need to isolate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span> To do this, we first subtract <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 36]</span> from both sides of the equation:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3kx + 36|= 8; 3kx + 36 \u2212 36|= 8 \u2212 36; 3kx|= \u2212 28]</span></p><p>Then, we divide both sides of the equation by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3k\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3kx|= \u2212 28; (3kx)/(3k)|= (\u2212 28)/(3k); (3kx)/(3k)|= (\u2212 28)/(3k); x|= \u2212 (28)/(3k)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by [MATH: 4] to get rid of the fraction:\n\n[MATH: (3)/(4)kx + 9|= 2; 4 \u22c5 ((3)/(4)kx + 9)|= 4 \u22c5 2; 3kx + 36|= 8]\n\nNow, we need to isolate [MATH: x.] To do this, we first subtract [MATH: 36] from both sides of the equation:\n\n[MATH: 3kx + 36|= 8; 3kx + 36 \u2212 36|= 8 \u2212 36; 3kx|= \u2212 28]\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 3k\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 3kx|= \u2212 28; (3kx)/(3k)|= (\u2212 28)/(3k); (3kx)/(3k)|= (\u2212 28)/(3k); x|= \u2212 (28)/(3k)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSolve the equation [MATH: \\dfrac 34 kx + 9 = 2] for the variable [MATH: x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by [MATH: 4] to get rid of the fraction:\n\n[MATH: (3)/(4)kx + 9|= 2; 4 \u22c5 ((3)/(4)kx + 9)|= 4 \u22c5 2; 3kx + 36|= 8]\n\nNow, we need to isolate [MATH: x.] To do this, we first subtract [MATH: 36] from both sides of the equation:\n\n[MATH: 3kx + 36|= 8; 3kx + 36 \u2212 36|= 8 \u2212 36; 3kx|= \u2212 28]\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 3k\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 3kx|= \u2212 28; (3kx)/(3k)|= (\u2212 28)/(3k); (3kx)/(3k)|= (\u2212 28)/(3k); x|= \u2212 (28)/(3k)]"
