          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We need to isolate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span> To do this, we first cross-multiply:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1)/(3)|= \u2212 (ax)/(5); (1)/(3)|= (\u2212 ax)/(5); 5 \u22c5 1|= 3 \u22c5 (\u2212 ax); 5|= \u2212 3ax]</span></p><p>Then, we divide both sides of the equation by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -3a\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5|= \u2212 3ax; (5)/(\u2212 3a)|= (\u2212 3ax)/(\u2212 3a); (5)/(\u2212 3a)|= (\u2212 3ax)/(\u2212 3a); \u2212 (5)/(3a)|= x; x|= \u2212 (5)/(3a)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We need to isolate [MATH: x.] To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n[MATH: (1)/(3)|= \u2212 (ax)/(5); (1)/(3)|= (\u2212 ax)/(5); 5 \u22c5 1|= 3 \u22c5 (\u2212 ax); 5|= \u2212 3ax]\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: -3a\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 5|= \u2212 3ax; (5)/(\u2212 3a)|= (\u2212 3ax)/(\u2212 3a); (5)/(\u2212 3a)|= (\u2212 3ax)/(\u2212 3a); \u2212 (5)/(3a)|= x; x|= \u2212 (5)/(3a)]",
